Visually instantly recognizable by its dark grey plating and oversized, bright red left forearm attachment, "Fiddler" takes the heavy-duty pneumatic hammer technology from Mark XXV ("Striker") and scales it down to a single arm. This unique asymmetrical design allowed the right side to retain full dexterity and precision repulsor control, while the reinforced left arm acted as a high-powered jackhammer for breach work and structural demolition.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXIX responds to the House Party Protocol call, engaging Extremis soldiers in close-quarters combat at the Norco oil rig before being destroyed during the final "Clean Slate" detonation order.
